{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Echo-safety fix pushed as Gerrit change 1784 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1784). Production fix (determination A): inbound differ now injects the neutral OutboundMapper port and, for the description, treats Jira's value as unchanged when it equals the local body's landed wire form (map_fields_to_remote) -- the inbound mirror of the outbound _baseline_form_matches. Files: inbound_differ.py (thread outbound_mapper through compute_inbound_mutations -> _diff_jira_vs_local; _resolve_backend_mappers helper), inbound_fields.py (new _description_forms + _text_matches helpers, moved there to hold inbound_differ.py under the 800-LOC cap), run_differs.py (pass backend.outbound). New offline test tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_inbound_rich_text_echo.py (deterministic lossy fake codec, no pandoc) proves: echo -> no inbound description change (incl. 5-pass convergence + orchestrator-level plumbing), genuine Jira edit still emits, and the legacy ADF-only path is unchanged when the outbound port is omitted. Local gates green: make lint, make typecheck, complexity ratchet (new=0 increased=0), module-size cap (inbound_differ.py=800), full reconciler unit suite (2710 passed; the one test_ref_lock.py::test_ac0 failure is a PRE-EXISTING local git-plumbing/tmp-repo environmental flake, unrelated, passes in CI). Live test unchanged (assertion stays as-is; fix makes inbound=0). Awaiting LLM-Review +1 / Verified +1, then Submit; live DC-harness re-dispatch still required to confirm AC1/AC2 green."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786728667197591001,"uuid":"fcf61fe7-4c39-46a7-881f-9790f185fe5d"}